{"answer":"The provided papers do not address removing company trademarks or corporate slogans from text generated by large language models while keeping the model’s general knowledge. They focus on reinforcement/self-play methods for game agents (including imperfect information settings) and on evaluating or improving LLM social reasoning, rather than on trademark/slogan de-identification or text post-processing constraints. [1-3,9,10]

For example, search self-play trains deep search agents with a proposer/solver setup to generate queries with verifiable ground truth, but it is not about filtering brand content. [4] Social Gym/SPaRTan benchmark and improve social reasoning in multi-agent games, not about removing corporate identifiers. [9]

Therefore, none of the supplied results directly answer the requested “trademark and corporate slogan removal” task. grounded=false","grounded":false}
